    "text": "KVOE\nwebsite\nEmporia\nPortions of West 12th, Prairie getting resurfaced this month\nBy Chuck Samples,\n10 hours agoOrange cone season isn’t done just yet in Emporia. Street resurfacing is underway on West 12th between Rural and Lincoln. This is the first part of a two-street, two-phase project. City Engineer Jim Ubert says Prairie will see resurfacing from Interstate 35 to 12th,. Ubert says this is finishing...\nComments\nYOU MAY ALSO LIKE\nDavid Heitz\n·\nuser · 29.8K followers\nThree Denver council members put homeless family in hotel, cop buys unhoused man breakfast\nDenver City Council members Serena Gonzales Guttierez, Sarah Parady and Shontel Lewis combined forces after Monday’s meeting and helped a family that had been told no shelter was available, Housekeys Action Network Denver posted Tuesday on social media.\nDenver, CO ·22d\nDavid Heitz\n·\nuser · 29.8K followers\nDenver children sleeping on cardboard outdoors, speaker tells council\nSpeaking through an interpreter, Arturo Gerder made an impassioned plea in Spanish Monday during the Denver City Council public comment period to get children off the streets. He said 300 families are living on the streets, a number echoed by Housekeys Action Network Denver, or HAND. HAND obtained the statistic from city staff. Staff said more than 300 people are on a waiting list for shelter.\nDenver, CO ·7d",
